{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/559884-missing-rite-of-the-spirit-brand","id":559884,"title":"Missing: Rite of the Spirit Brand","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-18T15:45:48-07:00","id":559884,"title":"Missing: Rite of the Spirit Brand","content":"So I can't help but notice that in the Core book, there is no Rite of the Spirit Brand. As this was one of the most important Rites in the old edition, I figured it would be in there, for some reason. Is the Rite of the Spirit Brand still necessary in order to get Renown? And if not, how does one go about that? You still get Renown brands, from the mechanics. So is this just an oversight, or am I missing an important mechanical change somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:00:47-07:00","id":559929,"title":"","content":"Lunes do it without rites now, it's mostly explained on p99 and onward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:26:24-07:00","id":559957,"title":"","content":"Sure, but how are the Lunes alerted in the first place? They don't come of their own accord, the character has to decide that this is the thing they want to use, and then get the lunes there so the Cahalith can sing it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:48:35-07:00","id":559965,"title":"","content":"If it's a great enough deed, the lunes will come to reward you for it. As servants of Luna that is part of their job, along with teaching Moon Gifts. You can help it along by having a Cahalith tell the tale, or boasting yourself, but Luna has an eye on almost everything involving her children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:49:32-07:00","id":560040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChanceTR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/559884-missing-rite-of-the-spirit-brand?p=559957#post559957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but how are the Lunes alerted in the first place? They don't come of their own accord, the character has to decide that this is the thing they want to use, and then get the lunes there so the Cahalith can sing it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many lunes have Influences in their chosen renown, if some glorious deed is happening, the Cahalith will feel it for example. Just like a spirit of violence can sense a bar brawl about to break out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:55:58-07:00","id":560044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChanceTR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/559884-missing-rite-of-the-spirit-brand?p=559957#post559957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but how are the Lunes alerted in the first place? They don't come of their own accord, the character has to decide that this is the thing they want to use, and then get the lunes there so the Cahalith can sing it up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lunes just know. It's best not to ask too many questions...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:58:46-07:00","id":560048,"title":"","content":"P69, 'Mother Luna watches over her children still, and they know it through the presence of Lunes, the mad moon spirits. Lunes judge the Oath, exalting its champions and condemning its transgressors.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T18:29:59-07:00","id":560127,"title":"","content":"If you really, really need a Lune on short notice, there's the Shadowcall ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:26:09-07:00","id":560277,"title":"","content":"But see, that seems to kind of contradict how it says raising renown works in the books. <br /> <br /> An Uratha might, soon after his First Change, undertake<br /> massive efforts to impress his peers. Many young Forsaken die<br /> less than a year after the First Change in efforts to impress<br /> their new families. Sometimes, success results in downright<br /> epic accomplishments that shower a young werewolf with<br /> Renown. The problem is, a character sets her own bar for<br /> Renown. With every increase, she raises that bar. To go<br /> further, she must improve upon her previous achievements.<br /> Some Uratha accomplish themselves into a proverbial corner<br /> this way; They do something so remarkable that they can\u2019t<br /> hope to do better. Particularly during character creation,<br /> consider how the character achieved her starting Renown<br /> dots. Did she shoot too high? Did she block herself out of<br /> future advancements? Or did she barely make the grade? (Were 99)<br /> <br /> So if it's the character (not the player, the character) that sets her own bar for Renown, then it makes no sense that the Lunes just magically come down and reward the person for things without them having to do anything for it. Does that make sense, or am I phrasing this badly? The Lunes can just know actions, sure, but the character has to specifically call them to acknowledge a particular act, of their choosing. So do they do that through Shadowbind? Or should there still be a Rite of the Spirit Brand? And if so, what Symbols would you suggest for creating one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:40:31-07:00","id":560290,"title":"","content":"There is no need for a rite of the Spirit Brand. The lunes can keep track of that sort of thing, since they can judge the worth of your act against your previous renown. If a lune wasn't there watching you, Luna is. And as god of the moon and shapechangers and spirits and mother of werewolves she'll know and send a lune to acknowledge your deed. Unless, possibly, you were born or acted beneath an eclipse.<br /> <br /> If you really want, something done at moonlight symbolizing brands and the five renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-18-2015, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T05:35:54-07:00","id":560670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChanceTR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/559884-missing-rite-of-the-spirit-brand?p=560277#post560277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if it's the character (not the player, the character) that sets her own bar for Renown, then it makes no sense that the Lunes just magically come down and reward the person for things without them having to do anything for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are doing things to attempt to attract the attention of the Lunes in order to earn Renown. The &quot;setting your own bar&quot; thing means that young Uratha can take great risks and do something really extraordinary and then struggle to top themselves to get the Lunes' attention again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}